      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well spotted @nasser.grainawi@oss.qualcomm.com. That tells me that we are indeed propagating this information from the wrong API endpoint.\n\nIt looks to me that performing _\"AI Review\"_ isn\u0027t a property of the change but rather an allowed/denied action.\n\nInstead of propagating this info from `ChangeInfo` it should be part of the `ChangeActions`.\n\nExample:\n\n```\nGET /changes/\u003cchange\u003e/revisions/\u003cpatchset\u003e/actions\n```\n\nReturns the list of actions that you can perform on a change.\n\n```\n{\n  \"cherrypick\": {\n    \"method\": \"POST\",\n    \"label\": \"Cherry Pick\",\n    \"title\": \"Cherry pick change to a different branch\",\n    \"enabled\": true\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee `GetRevisionActions` and the returned `Map\u003cString,ActionInfo\u003e`, WDYT?",
